WEBVTT

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.800
Looks like I've made something
rather entertaining.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.300
What is that, Jolly?

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.260
Perhaps I'll call it the
"Much Ado About Nothing Capriccio."

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.890
And now...

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.620
A jar breaks and sweet honey scatters

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.250
A jar breaks and sweet honey scatters

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.960
And spreads around my feet

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.170
A map that I've never seen before

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.930
Melts away and draws itself out

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.550
Something is about to awaken

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.390
I hide a knife within my chest

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.060
I put poisoned lipgloss on my lips

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.860
My gaze is uncaptured but bewildered

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.030
I want to change starting today

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:17.650
I point a gun at my lifeless past

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:22.530
I want to escape from the world of mirrors

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:23.790
Take me Higher

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.620
Take me to Heaven

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.210
I don't care if I can't go back

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:33.000
I want to see a world that I don't know

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.260
I break the doorknob and the chain

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:40.340
And run into the magenta morning

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.210
"To thank you for all that you've done,

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.880
I've prepared a little gift for you.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.970
Please come to the dining hall."

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:22.890
It must be from Fel.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.060
Hey, Nova!

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:32.060
An invitation from Bambina
makes it worth getting up early.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:37.690
How thoughtful of Milady to surprise us with gifts.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.280
Cioccolato!

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.160
They look delicious!

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.950
They're very cute gifts.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.330
I don't know about that.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:52.120
Cioccolato is an aphrodisiac of amore.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.250
I like it. It stirs me up.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.880
Milady...

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:59.590
Well then, with gratitude for Milady...

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.180
Thank you for the treat!

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:10.020
This tastes a little...

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.820
Libertá! Libertá!

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.030
What? I'm calling myself?

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.200
Get a hold of yourself!

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.160
Am I dreaming?

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:26.330
Just look!

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.040
I'm...

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.080
Nova?!

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.420
Damn it, he's not gonna get away with this.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.210
The only one who could do something
like this is that alchemist geezer.

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.050
Luca?

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:44.510
To think he actually had the nerve
to involve me, as well.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.140
Just look at how fluffy my hair is, thanks to him.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.020
And instead, I'm smooth as can be.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:52.980
This makes no sense.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.150
What the hell happened to everyone?

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.610
This is what happened...

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.780
I am Luca.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.780
I'm Debito.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.740
I'm Pace.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.570
I'm Dante.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.370
I'm Nova.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:14.460
We were tricked into taking
Jolly's personality swapping potion.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.000
Personality swapping potion?

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:18.540
Indeed. The personality swapping potion

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.760
separates one's soul, or personality,
from that person,

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.130
and puts it in someone else's body.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.930
Separates our personalities?!

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:26.840
Indeed.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.850
It was a very rare potion, so I remember it well.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.350
Where did you see it?

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.940
I believe I saw it in one of the books
in Jolly's alchemy lab.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:37.980
Then we'll just have to
kill the old man and steal it.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.060
Please wait.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.940
Knowing him, that wouldn't end it.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:44.700
No kidding.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:48.070
It's probably best that we don't let Jolly find out
that his potion actually worked.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:51.080
Please act like you didn't take the potion

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.700
and carry on the rest of the day
as you normally would.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.330
Meanwhile, I will try to find a way
to turn us back to normal.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.210
Oh, no! Look at the time.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.500
I must prepare tea for Milady!

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.090
I guess I better go, then.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:06.550
Why are you going?!

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.720
We're carrying on as we normally would, right?

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.180
That would make me Bambina's attendant today.

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.060
Feel free to take the day off at the Coins today.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.600
Just hurry up and find us an antidote.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.730
Don't worry.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:22.070
Despite how he looks, Debito is a gentleman.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.070
Yep. No need to hurry at all.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:28.360
It's not actually a bad thing,
living as someone else for a while.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:29.490
Right?

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.240
Yep.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:36.830
All right! Another day filled with Regalo sunshine!

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:40.710
Sir Nova, are we really starting
our patrol from up here today?

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:44.880
This is quite different from our usual route...

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.210
It's fine, it's fine!

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:48.760
This is more fun, isn't it?

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:55.890
I believe there's a phrase from Giappone:
"Idiots and something else like high places."

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.180
Looks like it's true.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.770
Oh, you came, too?

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:02.270
Guess you're pretty bored.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:03.230
This is my job.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:06.360
I can't have you making any more trouble.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:10.740
Take a look.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.410
From up here, if there's any trouble,
you can see it instantly.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.200
You'd be able to get there quickly, too.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.290
The purpose of patrolling is to
interact with the citizens

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.540
and to nip any arguments in the bud
before they can start.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.420
You can't understand how the people live
just by looking down on them.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.130
However...

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:34.680
That is a nice breeze.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:40.440
If you run, it feels like you're flying!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:41.190
Eh?

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:43.020
Come on!

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:44.690
You guys, too!

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.030
Yes, sir.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.200
Come on! What's keeping you?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.160
Hey! Look in front of you!

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.340
Ow...

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:11.220
Why do things like this always
happen when I'm with him?

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:17.430
You must really like falling onto
people's stands, don't you?

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:19.980
What do you mean?

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:24.190
Step right up! Hey, Signorina!
How about a scarf?

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.320
Come on! Start saying stuff!

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:28.110
Huh?

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.990
W-Welcome...

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.910
The hell was that?!
Do you intend to do this or not?

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.330
Welcome!

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:38.990
See? You can do it if you try.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.290
Hey, what are you doing here?

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.540
You never showed up,
so we were looking for you.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:50.420
You promised you'd tell us more
of that story from the other day.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:51.630
Story?

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:54.260
The story about Libertá the Hero!

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:56.180
Oh, man. I totally forgot!

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:58.180
You heard 'em. Get going.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:00.270
Why should I...

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:03.940
Come on, let's go!

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:04.770
Let's go!

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:07.480
Let's go! Let's go!

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:08.650
Yay! Story!
Let's go! Let's go!

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.270
Yay! Story!

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:13.860
Hey! The fish I got from you was rotten!

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.490
That stuff put me in the hospital!

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:16.870
What're you gonna do about it?

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:19.280
B-But our fish is...

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.410
What's wrong?

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:22.040
Mr. Nova!

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.290
Samurai Nova?!

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.590
It wasn't in this one, either.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:41.600
Oh, no! I must prepare Milady's afternoon tea!

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:48.230
That's right... Today that is
Debito's job, not mine.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.200
Right now, the two of them must be...

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.240
The two of them?!

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:02.660
No, no... Despite how he looks,
Debito is a gentleman.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:06.080
He would never do anything
inappropriate to Milady...

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.630
Right, he'd never...

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.460
How does your tea taste today, Milady?

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:19.180
It tastes a little different than usual, but it's good.

00:09:19.180 --> 00:09:20.140
Thank you.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.720
How unfortunate.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:22.350
Huh?

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:23.850
I'd hoped you'd say today's...

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:29.440
or rather, that my tea
was especially delicious today.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:31.440
Um, Luca, your face is really close.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:38.030
Recently, I feel restless when we
have tea together like this.

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.450
You do?

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:47.410
Yes. You don't even understand how I feel
during these precious moments.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.460
How sinful of me...

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:55.010
Milady, I want to be your special one.

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:56.550
Special?

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.430
Indeed.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:03.310
The only one to appear in those
beautiful green eyes of yours...

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:04.560
Debito!

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:06.680
Debito?

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:09.440
Milady! Please run!

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.230
Huh? What?
Milady! Please run!

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:10.730
Huh? What?
Debi... I mean, Luca, get over here!

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:12.770
Debi... I mean, Luca, get over here!

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:14.320
Ugh. You're so annoying.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.990
I was just about to have some
adult time with Bambina...

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:22.490
Mommy, look at that guy.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:24.200
Shh! Don't look!

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:32.040
<i>I had almost forgotten this sensation!</i>

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.880
<i>This feeling between my fingers!</i>

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.630
Yes, yes, yes!

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:42.510
<i>Oh, to have hair again...</i>

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:49.930
So, how does it feel to have hair again?

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:51.730
I want to thank my Hairvenly Father!

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.400
You know, for my hair. Just kidding!

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:05.200
Mr. Pace.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.250
I'm going to make sure you pay your tab today.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:10.910
Tab?

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:13.630
<i>Damn that Pace...</i>

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:19.920
<i>But I guess I'll pay it for him,</i>
<i>since this hair puts me in such a great mood.</i>

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.260
How much is it?

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:23.840
Uh...

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.140
Come on, get to washing!

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.560
Why must I do something like this?

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:36.060
Well, it's pretty rare for you to eat
so much, Mr. Dante.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:37.070
Huh?

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.150
Oh, here's the payment.

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:41.950
Also, would you take care of my...

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:45.030
I mean, Pace's tab while you're at it?

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:46.830
Are you sure?

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.910
The tab of a family member is my tab, as well.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.160
I'll pay that tab, and it'll be totally... tabular!

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:55.130
Nothing less from you, Mr. Dante.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:56.920
Your puns are top notch today!

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:03.340
J-Just kidding...

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:08.810
I have some rather unfortunate news.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.850
I have not found a way to make the antidote.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.520
That's not good enough!

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:15.400
I've had enough of babysitting children!

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:17.190
True.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:20.360
I guess we can't stay in
someone else's body forever...

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:25.160
There is only one book in Regalo that
describes how to make the antidote,

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.780
and it can only be in Jolly's library.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:29.830
Which means we'll have to kill
the old man after all.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:31.080
But we can't.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:34.040
If we do that, all of our hard work
today will be for nothing.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:36.540
You haven't worked hard at all.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.080
Oh, right.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:40.090
Then what are we going to do?

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:43.130
This leaves us with only one option...

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.720
We'll have to steal the book out of Jolly's library.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.650
Sounds like the old man's practicing his cello.

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:01.230
How very sophisticated.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:05.860
Hopefully, he'll stay put until Luca and
the others get back from the alchemy lab.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:10.450
He's coming out!

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:12.790
This isn't good. Someone stall him.

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:13.870
That won't be me.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.210
I can't, either!

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:17.120
You idiots! Stop pushi...

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.750
G-Good evening, Jolly.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:28.180
I never knew you had skills like that, Luca.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:32.260
When you're the apprentice of that man,
you go through a lot of hardships.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:35.770
Well then, I'll be inside searching for the book.

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:37.310
So please, keep an eye out.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:38.440
Understood.

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:39.270
Yeah!

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:44.110
It's rather rare for you to talk to me.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.150
Is that not allowed?

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:51.990
It is. Oh, about your friend with the eyepatch...

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:53.700
Debito?

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:54.700
Indeed.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:14:00.880
I hear he's been seducing women
to come to the casino.

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.250
I'm happy that he's bringing in money,

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:09.220
but don't you think such a vulgar business
is rather suiting for a man with no class?

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.970
Debito! Endure! Endure it!

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:18.770
I hear he's been bragging that
there's no woman he can't seduce,

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:22.980
but if you ask me, he's no better
than a starving stray dog.

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:24.650
Hang in there! Hang in there!

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:29.900
To think that he's satisfied with
women who fall for those silly lines...

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:35.080
I find the tales of his exploits
to be rather sketchy...

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:37.330
This is what I get for letting you talk.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:39.460
Don't push it, old man.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:43.040
What's the matter, Luca?

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.880
The way you're talking almost sounds like De...

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.460
Found you, Luca!

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:52.300
H-Hey, Jolly. Beautiful night, isn't it?

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.430
Want to play hide and seek?

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.220
Hide and seek?

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.770
That's fine with me...

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:05.190
I can show you what happens when I get serious.

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:09.440
I-I'm kidding... Totally kidding. Just kidding!

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:12.860
<i>I know, I'll say some pun...</i>

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:16.740
<i>I can't think of anything!</i>

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.870
This isn't it... neither is this.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.580
I must hurry and find it...

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:29.550
Isn't he done yet?
Maybe I should go help him.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:32.510
Don't. You won't be of any help, anyway.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:34.260
What do you mean by that?

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:37.560
Just do the job you were given.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.970
Talk about stubborn.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.770
That's why you never grow.

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.150
What is he doing?

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:50.280
I guess I have no choice.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.950
I'll have to step in as the director...

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:55.110
H-Huh? What's everyone doing?

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:00.120
I'm sorry.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:05.080
Well, well... It's unusual for your
stomach to growl, Mr. Director.

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:08.170
Oh, I have just the thing.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:11.210
It's not here, not here, not here...

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.550
Move, chickpea!

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.380
That doesn't apply today!

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:17.430
Yeah, I bet you're happy about that,
since you're in my body!

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:21.100
I feel like your stupidity is seeping in,
and it's very unpleasant!

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.850
You two...

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:26.400
I asked you two to guard the door, did I not?

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:28.980
We're sorry...

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:30.530
Lasagna!

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:34.240
Martha brought it up for me a little while ago.

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:38.780
However, I don't usually eat this late,
so I thought I'd give it to Pace...

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:42.080
But I don't mind giving it to you, Mr. Director.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:43.200
Yay!

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:44.500
You idiot!

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.330
Who knows what's in there this time?

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:49.250
"This time"?

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:54.550
You make it sound as though
I've done that before...

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:58.430
Lasagna...

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:03.640
Want to eat... lasagna...

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:05.940
Wait! Calm down...

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:08.190
Lasagna!

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:15.950
What is it?

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:19.660
Today, after you left,
while I was working at the shop,

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:22.410
this guy tried to cause trouble at another shop.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.750
But when they saw my...

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:30.130
no, your face, they took off.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:33.550
It must be the result of your daily patrols.

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:35.550
They were talking about you at the market, too.

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:39.510
They say they can all live peacefully
because you're around.

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:43.350
They're overreacting.

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:49.060
Those kids look up to you, as well.

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.860
Not just those two,

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:56.070
but other kids also gathered
as soon as they saw your face.

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:58.570
The same goes for my subordinates.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:04.410
Libertá, the people around you
are always smiling.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:08.660
I found that out after being you all day today.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:14.800
It means some good came out
of this ridiculous switch.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.210
Yeah.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:20.930
This month's motto: Patrol from
the point of view of the chickpea.

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:21.840
What?

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:23.930
Nothing less from a little kid.

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:27.430
Your work ethic is down to Earth
since you're barely off the ground.

00:18:27.430 --> 00:18:31.520
I'm going to lower my line of sight and make sure
I treasure my interactions with the citizens...

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:34.020
Why you...

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.070
...genuine idiot!

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:38.690
Found i-...

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:46.450
You two...

00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:48.620
My bad...

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.120
I apologize.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:54.460
Sorry, I ate it...

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:59.300
Now that you've finished eating
your lasagna, Mr. Director,

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:01.260
I believe you owe me an explanation.

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:02.340
An explanation?

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:07.270
According to my observations,
all of your actions today...

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:11.890
I must say they were quite peculiar.

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:13.270
For example...

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:18.030
As well as...

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.870
There was also this...

00:19:28.290 --> 00:19:32.290
Now, will you be good and talk, or...

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.340
Let's go.

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.760
Oh, look at the time.

00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:43.380
I need to eat lasagna!

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:45.180
See ya, Jolly.

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:47.310
Buonanotte!

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:53.440
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:57.190
If we all drink this together,
we'll return to normal.

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:04.410
Well, then...

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:08.080
Oh, no! I've spilled the precious potion...

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:11.330
Oh, what are you doing?

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:13.210
There's no point if we don't
all drink it together.

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:17.000
<i>Sorry, everyone... Just one more day.</i>

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:18.920
<i>I want to stay fluffy just one more day.</i>

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.250
Not to worry.

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:21.960
I've made extra.

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:23.090
Huh?

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:26.340
All right, let's try this again. Salu...

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.350
Oh, my hand slipped again.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:32.270
What's wrong with you, Dante?

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:34.350
Could it be that you...

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:39.820
No, I... it's not like I want to stay fluffy
a little longer or anything...

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:43.740
It's fine. Spill as much as you like.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:47.370
All right, one last time.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:49.450
Salute!

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:51.160
Salute...

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:59.250
Did something fun happen?

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:00.250
Indeed.

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:04.920
<i>Any moment now...</i>

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.970
All right! We're back to nor...

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:15.020
Damn it, now I'm really going to kill
that alchemist geezer...

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:16.890
Huh? That's me?

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:19.810
Hey, I'm Debito now.

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:22.230
This was a fake.

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:25.740
I never thought he'd go this far...

00:21:26.070 --> 00:21:29.870
I wonder when we'll be back to normal...

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.120
If Debito and I switched this time,

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:34.910
and Luca and Pace switched, that means...

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.120
Why...

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:38.750
Nova?

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:43.090
Libertá! If you're his apprentice,
do something about that!

00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:45.630
I can't watch this anymore!

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:49.390
Sweet, so I'm Nova now.

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:52.970
This is great. On top of being fluffy,
it's shiny and sleek.

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:55.060
And his skin glistens and feels so smooth...

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:57.060
Almost as smooth as the
personality swapped into him.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:58.810
Just kidding!

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:20.000
A wandering shadow on a stone paving

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:27.470
The wind blows fiercely trying to tear it away

00:22:28.010 --> 00:22:33.220
Within an invisible enclosure

00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:40.270
We just kept looking up at the endless sky

00:22:40.270 --> 00:22:47.030
We decide to go far away

00:22:47.030 --> 00:22:52.740
With the shoes we can't slip off still on our hearts

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:57.950
Try We run off

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:01.920
Holding onto our broken down dreams

00:23:01.920 --> 00:23:05.340
We won't be lost anymore

00:23:05.340 --> 00:23:07.130
Pieces of treasure

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.840
If we can still shine after falling in a frenzy

00:23:09.840 --> 00:23:14.100
If we can still shine after falling in a frenzy

00:23:14.300 --> 00:23:20.270
Even a shattered piece can be a

00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:23.850
Treasure
